  "description": "BAMQOX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C44 H62 Mn2 N4 O26 Tm4,C4 H10 O1,2(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tm1 (Tm) has 7 O neighbors; Tm2 (Tm) has 7 O neighbors; Tm3 (Tm) has 7 O neighbors; Tm4 (Tm) has 7 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.851-4.021 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.88-143.59°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C50H80N4Mn2O29Tm4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 8 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Mn(III), Tm(III).",
